Feature: The flight display of the TX15
  The screen of the TX15 shows the flight in the layout of the ArduPilot telemetry script of
  Yaapu. On top are the flight mode (big, with ARMED or DISARMED beside it), the satellites,
  the link and the battery. In the middle is an artificial horizon that banks and pitches with
  the plane, with the airspeed, the ground speed and the heading on its left, and the height
  above home, the climb and the distance to home on its right. The battery has a bar. The last
  messages of ArduPilot are along the bottom: a PreArm check that fails, a new mode, a failsafe.

  Expectation: The screen shows the airspeed
    Given the TX15 screen airspeed is 18 m/s
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen airspeed is at least 17.5 m/s
    And the TX15 screen airspeed is at most 18.5 m/s

  Expectation: The screen shows the climb with its sign
    Given the TX15 screen climb is -3 m/s
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen climb is at least -3.2 m/s
    And the TX15 screen climb is at most -2.8 m/s

  Expectation: The screen counts the satellites
    Given the TX15 screen satellites is 9
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen satellites is 9

  Expectation: The screen shows what ArduPilot says
    A PreArm check that fails is the most useful message when the plane will not arm. The
    message is in MAVLink, down the same serial line, and the screen reads it from there.
    Given the TX15 screen message is PreArm: Throttle (RC3) is not neutral
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the TX15 screen message is PreArm: Throttle (RC3) is not neutral
